<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:37Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Ceuta: EU grants Spain €115 million in emergency aid</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:106b0e05789a13bd53351fcef57051baed53def25b2223d714600f1b15066bd5</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T17:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ceuta-eu-grants-spain-_115-million-in-emergency-aid/a-79206505--754cf3a038a5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ceuta-eu-grants-spain-€115-million-in-emergency-aid/a-79206505?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU has said the funds will go toward bolstering border security and returning migrants to Morocco. The move comes in the wake of a crisis that saw more than 70,000 migrants overwhelm the Spanish exclave in July.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia's constitutional reform: What does it mean — especially for Abiy?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:544a644c6a2cf6a993cfd897aea8d8bf3e1bb1b24e0c40b04a0638653b7e3fdc</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T15:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-s-constitutional-reform-what-does-it-mean-especially-for-abiy/a-79172262--7aa1de37183a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-s-constitutional-reform-what-does-it-mean-especially-for-abiy/a-79172262?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ethiopian Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed stands to benefit from a planned constitutional reform in the country. A new presidential system would reshape political power — and could give him a more powerful mandate in office.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Trafficked into fraud: An African crisis situation in Cambodia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:372e9691737e68a41488661b7518a4711aa0effb9f32de54573a802040f607c0</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T08:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trafficked-into-fraud-an-african-crisis-situation-in-cambodia/a-79189967--d423991a2cca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trafficked-into-fraud-an-african-crisis-situation-in-cambodia/a-79189967?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Cambodia's crackdown on scam operators is stranding young African trafficking victims in the Asian country with no money, no passport and no prospects.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Morocco earthquake 3 years on: 'No one has remembered us'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:798b99283bf1d0ad64de99a80dd603d18b75456994127e5ddebb7d594a8a9877</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T18:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/morocco-earthquake-3-years-on-no-one-has-remembered-us/a-78874844--cbd4f3eb032b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/morocco-earthquake-3-years-on-no-one-has-remembered-us/a-78874844?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Morocco has rebuilt thousands of homes since the 2023 earthquake. But some survivors are still living in tents and say they have received no state aid.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>How climate change and food insecurity could fuel future conflicts</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e31380a422208f75e891baa1c3061c9322499de1dd9686ee8f3abb65398110d9</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T07:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-climate-change-and-food-insecurity-could-fuel-future-conflicts/a-78871431--8e63f64c4115.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-climate-change-and-food-insecurity-could-fuel-future-conflicts/a-78871431?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Climate change, conflict, and trade tensions are putting pressure on the global food system. New research suggests the biggest risk is not food shortages, but whether societies can peacefully adapt to change.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
